      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "**Question:** What is caching?"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Short Answer"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Caching stores frequently accessed data in fast storage to reduce database load and improve response times."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Detailed Explanation"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Cache types: in-memory, distributed (Redis), CDN. Cache strategies: read-through, write-through, write-behind. Handle cache invalidation carefully."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Example"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "Caching Example",
        "language": "csharp",
        "code": "// In-memory cache\npublic class ProductService {\n    private readonly IMemoryCache _cache;\n    \n    public async Task<Product> GetProduct(int id) {\n        return await _cache.GetOrCreateAsync($\"product_{id}\", entry => {\n            entry.SlidingExpiration = TimeSpan.FromMinutes(10);\n            return _db.Products.FindAsync(id);\n        });\n    }\n}"
      }
